WEBVTT

00:00:00.461 --> 00:00:03.381
I'm firmly against the idea of transferring

00:00:03.381 --> 00:00:05.817
Cynical Molco's rights to Seo Design!

00:00:05.817 --> 00:00:09.185
Ms. Kusakabe only cares
about money and numbers.

00:00:09.185 --> 00:00:13.457
I don't want Molco
anywhere near someone like that.

00:00:13.457 --> 00:00:18.100
She doesn't have any love for characters!

00:00:21.597 --> 00:00:24.766
Don't. Mr. Seo, don't!

00:00:29.801 --> 00:00:35.066
I'll never forgive anyone who hurts O-Con!

00:00:35.725 --> 00:00:41.053
You were just yelling that O-Con
doesn't have any love for characters,

00:00:41.053 --> 00:00:44.717
but who are you to her?
Family? Her best friend?

00:00:44.717 --> 00:00:48.649
- No, that's not it...
- No? Then what was all that earlier?

00:00:48.649 --> 00:00:49.649
[Prince, what's wrong with you?]
Pure imagination?

00:00:49.649 --> 00:00:51.599
[So scary; Where are his manners?]
You shout passionately with just that?

00:00:51.599 --> 00:00:52.929
[Is this his true nature? He is not a prince]

00:00:52.929 --> 00:00:53.929
[He's like a totally different person now]
Well...

00:00:53.929 --> 00:00:57.133
[Give me back my feels!]
Besides, if O-Con doesn't love characters,

00:00:57.133 --> 00:01:00.461
then why does she get angry,
laugh, and cry over them?

00:01:00.461 --> 00:01:03.933
Isn't that love? Hey, isn't that love?

00:01:05.113 --> 00:01:06.465
Then take back what you just said.

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:10.041
Give me the camera! Hand it over!

00:01:10.041 --> 00:01:11.369
All right, here we go.

00:01:11.369 --> 00:01:13.045
Say that you made it all up
and got overly dramatic.

00:01:13.045 --> 00:01:16.597
Here we go! Three, two, one, action!

00:01:16.597 --> 00:01:19.097
Well...

00:01:19.097 --> 00:01:20.600
Why are you crying?

00:01:20.600 --> 00:01:22.617
I just want you to take back what you said.
Let's try that again.

00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:25.053
- Okay, three, two, action!
- Mr. Seo, that's enough!

00:01:25.053 --> 00:01:27.469
- Mr. Seo, please stop already!
- Hey, stop! Focus!

00:01:27.469 --> 00:01:29.177
Let go! My back...

00:01:29.177 --> 00:01:31.097
- Ouch, ouch! Stop, stop!
- She insulted O-Con!

00:01:31.097 --> 00:01:32.853
- She attacked O-Con!
- Stop, stop, stop!

00:01:32.853 --> 00:01:34.297
- Take it back!
- Stop, stop, stop!

00:01:34.297 --> 00:01:36.400
Take back your passionate shout!

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:39.433
Here we go! Viewers, let's roll!

00:01:39.433 --> 00:01:40.465
[He's the worst;
Fake prince; Totally lost it]

00:01:40.465 --> 00:01:42.165
[This guy is unhinged; I feel bad for Tuesla]

00:01:43.069 --> 00:01:46.997
- Take it back!
- Disqualified!

00:01:49.241 --> 00:01:54.865
I will never forgive anyone
who threatens Molco's happiness.

00:01:57.973 --> 00:02:01.769
Mizuki Seo, you are disqualified.

00:02:01.769 --> 00:02:04.553
- What? Why me?
- Please wait!

00:02:04.553 --> 00:02:07.345
Please, continue the evaluation
until the end!

00:02:07.345 --> 00:02:08.777
Mr. Seo isn't at fault here. I am.

00:02:08.777 --> 00:02:09.925
It's all my fault, so please...

00:02:09.925 --> 00:02:12.566
Are you admitting that Rena's claim is true?

00:02:15.389 --> 00:02:20.300
I am truly sorry.

00:02:24.300 --> 00:02:25.400
[She admitted it! Corrupt, greedy consultant]

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:26.809
[She probably doesn't even care
about ruining other people's lives]

00:02:26.809 --> 00:02:29.817
I cannot entrust Molco to someone

00:02:29.817 --> 00:02:32.837
who loses their temper
and their mind in anger.

00:02:32.837 --> 00:02:36.077
And the same applies to Rena.

00:02:36.077 --> 00:02:40.121
Therefore, everyone, please step over here.

00:02:40.121 --> 00:02:42.973
[Certificate of Rights]

00:02:45.229 --> 00:02:46.689
Mr. Nimura.

00:02:46.689 --> 00:02:48.905
All right.

00:02:48.905 --> 00:02:53.241
Please take good care of Cynical Molco.

00:02:53.241 --> 00:02:56.353
I accept with the utmost gratitude.

00:02:57.901 --> 00:03:00.773
The winner of the Cynical Molco
Proposal Competition is

00:03:00.773 --> 00:03:03.449
Kazuo Nimura of Peace Plus!

00:03:03.449 --> 00:03:05.657
- Congratulations.
- Thank you very much.

00:03:09.801 --> 00:03:12.029
I...

00:03:12.029 --> 00:03:14.025
Rena.

00:03:14.025 --> 00:03:15.929
You must have been scared.

00:03:18.037 --> 00:03:22.601
Indeed, we can rest easy
leaving Molco in your hands, Mr. Nimura.

00:03:22.601 --> 00:03:25.297
I will do everything I can
to meet your expectations...

00:03:25.297 --> 00:03:27.033
What's this?

00:03:27.033 --> 00:03:28.769
Oh, well... That's...

00:03:28.769 --> 00:03:31.600
What is the meaning of this, Mr. Omishima?

00:03:32.677 --> 00:03:35.157
This memo was in Rena's possession.

00:03:35.157 --> 00:03:40.253
Everything Rena just claimed earlier
is written down right here.

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:42.225
And at the bottom, it says,

00:03:42.225 --> 00:03:45.373
"If you can get Mizuki Seo
caught in a scandal,

00:03:45.373 --> 00:03:48.653
you will be paid a bonus."

00:03:48.653 --> 00:03:51.165
So, what does this mean?

00:03:51.165 --> 00:03:54.669
- I have no recollection of this at all.
- Was this rigged from the start?

00:03:54.669 --> 00:03:59.869
Perhaps Rena wrote her own
personal wishes on that note.

00:04:01.941 --> 00:04:03.865
I can't do this.

00:04:04.629 --> 00:04:06.481
An act like this...

00:04:07.297 --> 00:04:09.237
I can't keep doing this!

00:04:09.237 --> 00:04:12.153
- What are you talking about...
- All of it...

00:04:12.153 --> 00:04:14.873
- It was all rigged!
- What is the meaning of this?

00:04:14.873 --> 00:04:17.809
- No, I...
- We took this competition seriously!

00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:19.269
- Quit messing around!
- Exactly!

00:04:19.269 --> 00:04:20.767
- Explain yourself!
- Mr. Omishima,

00:04:20.767 --> 00:04:22.257
please give us an explanation!

00:04:22.257 --> 00:04:25.365
Was this entire competition staged?

00:04:25.365 --> 00:04:27.097
- Is that true?
- It was decided from the start, right?

00:04:27.097 --> 00:04:28.966
Explain yourself!

00:04:45.853 --> 00:04:49.037
It's this side of you that...

00:04:49.825 --> 00:04:52.193
- Mr. Seo!
- Mr. Omishima!

00:04:55.973 --> 00:04:58.553
[METI Buildings]
You two are in the middle of a scandal.

00:04:58.553 --> 00:05:01.133
We are truly sorry.

00:05:02.893 --> 00:05:06.105
Regarding Tutu-Tuesla's appointment
as Expo Ambassador,

00:05:06.105 --> 00:05:09.381
as things stand,
we have no choice but to revoke it.

00:05:09.381 --> 00:05:12.313
Unless there's a dramatic plan
to restore your reputation.

00:05:12.313 --> 00:05:15.697
A dramatic plan to restore our reputation.

00:05:15.697 --> 00:05:17.525
As soon as possible.

00:05:21.669 --> 00:05:25.465
Don't worry. It's not officially revoked yet.

00:05:26.809 --> 00:05:30.345
Wow, did you see that?
The fake prince and the greedy consultant.

00:05:30.345 --> 00:05:33.473
Wait! No! We can't take any more scandal.

00:05:34.813 --> 00:05:36.185
Dramatic restoration of our reputation.

00:05:36.185 --> 00:05:40.000
Dramatic restoration of our reputation.

00:05:40.000 --> 00:05:42.133
[Kitchen Sakoda]

00:05:46.557 --> 00:05:48.937
Sorry, it's me.

00:05:48.937 --> 00:05:50.717
What's up?

00:05:50.717 --> 00:05:53.133
Well, I heard you're closing the restaurant.

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:57.266
Oh! Sorry, I was planning on
telling you properly.

00:05:58.617 --> 00:06:03.973
Look, the restaurant failing
was because of my own shortcomings.

00:06:03.973 --> 00:06:06.297
It wasn't your fault.

00:06:06.297 --> 00:06:08.305
You're going to have something to eat, right?

00:06:08.305 --> 00:06:11.265
- But...
- It's fine. Just eat.

00:06:11.265 --> 00:06:13.657
Maybe it's because I'm finally free
from the stress of running a business.

00:06:13.657 --> 00:06:15.993
My back feels great.

00:06:15.993 --> 00:06:17.873
Quitting isn't all bad.

00:06:17.873 --> 00:06:21.286
Good things can come out of it too.

00:06:23.773 --> 00:06:30.200
Good things can come out of quitting.

00:06:31.141 --> 00:06:35.300
Here is the dramatic plan to restore
our reputation that I came up with.

00:06:36.717 --> 00:06:40.569
I, Anna Kusakabe, and Seo Design

00:06:40.569 --> 00:06:43.729
will terminate our consulting contract.

00:06:56.125 --> 00:06:58.373
[Notice of Contract Termination]
You mean you're leaving us?

00:06:58.373 --> 00:07:00.136
The Expo Ambassador role

00:07:00.136 --> 00:07:01.653
[Episode 9]
is an unprecedented opportunity

00:07:01.653 --> 00:07:04.389
to introduce Tuesla to people
around the world.

00:07:04.389 --> 00:07:07.329
We must avoid having it canceled
over this scandal at all costs.

00:07:07.329 --> 00:07:09.461
But Mr. Seo is caught in a scandal too.

00:07:09.461 --> 00:07:14.501
As for Mr. Seo, since his outburst
was triggered by Mr. Omishima's scheme,

00:07:14.501 --> 00:07:17.173
and he risked himself to save Molco
from falling into that pool,

00:07:17.173 --> 00:07:20.489
many people are viewing him
in a positive light.

00:07:20.489 --> 00:07:21.613
Meanwhile, regarding me...

00:07:21.613 --> 00:07:25.365
"How can that consultant show her face
after ruining someone's family?"

00:07:25.365 --> 00:07:28.649
- "Get out of the industry already..."
- Okay, that's enough. Stop.

00:07:28.649 --> 00:07:32.605
My scandal is at a point
where it can't be put out.

00:07:32.605 --> 00:07:36.505
So we claim that Mr. Seo's
crazy behavior at the competition

00:07:36.505 --> 00:07:39.469
was all done under my instructions.

00:07:39.469 --> 00:07:42.097
Concentrate all the scandal elements
on me alone.

00:07:42.097 --> 00:07:45.621
And then terminate my contract.
That would be the best move.

00:07:45.621 --> 00:07:48.337
Returns haven't stopped coming in since then.

00:07:48.337 --> 00:07:51.645
If we don't act fast,
the damage will be irreversible.

00:07:52.629 --> 00:07:55.600
Wait... Hey!

00:07:58.241 --> 00:08:00.009
Did you forget?

00:08:00.009 --> 00:08:02.453
Our contract was for you to create a big hit.

00:08:02.453 --> 00:08:03.481
But we're nowhere near that.

00:08:03.481 --> 00:08:04.761
And you want to terminate the contract?

00:08:04.761 --> 00:08:07.013
Terminating the contract is necessary
to make it a big hit.

00:08:07.013 --> 00:08:08.483
- That's why this is...
- Then do you have

00:08:08.483 --> 00:08:10.845
another plan to restore our reputation?

00:08:10.845 --> 00:08:13.901
A plan that will stop our scandal.

00:08:16.161 --> 00:08:17.966
Well...

00:08:21.985 --> 00:08:26.021
I'm sorry, but this requires
an urgent response.

00:08:26.689 --> 00:08:29.509
Please give me your decision by tomorrow.

00:08:29.509 --> 00:08:33.705
I'll think of one! A plan to
restore our reputation! By tomorrow!

00:08:33.705 --> 00:08:36.133
We approached Mr. Nimura of Peace Plus again

00:08:36.133 --> 00:08:38.769
regarding the transfer of
Cynical Molco's rights,

00:08:38.769 --> 00:08:41.013
but he withdrew his intention
to acquire them.

00:08:41.013 --> 00:08:44.477
Cynical Molco is practically a liability now.

00:08:44.477 --> 00:08:48.041
Now, about how you will
take responsibility for this...

00:08:48.041 --> 00:08:51.637
Then first, allow me to present to everyone

00:08:51.637 --> 00:08:53.889
a proposal for the restructuring of Merry.

00:08:53.889 --> 00:08:56.321
Please give me five minutes of your time.

00:08:58.113 --> 00:09:00.037
Please begin.

00:09:01.837 --> 00:09:04.629
What are you doing? Hurry up with the video.

00:09:04.629 --> 00:09:07.977
I have already informed Mr. Shiiba.

00:09:07.977 --> 00:09:12.597
I want him to keep working hard
as a secretary under the new president too.

00:09:14.457 --> 00:09:16.400
Thank you for your hard work.

00:09:27.745 --> 00:09:29.533
I'm fine.

00:09:41.501 --> 00:09:44.609
[Dramatic Restoration Plan, Mizuki Seo]
Here is Dramatic Restoration Plan.

00:09:44.609 --> 00:09:48.001
Donating All Sales of Tuesla to Charity.

00:09:48.001 --> 00:09:50.669
By donating all of Tuesla's sales somewhere,

00:09:50.669 --> 00:09:52.697
- we restore our reputation...
- Rejected.

00:09:52.697 --> 00:09:54.802
The cheap ulterior motive of trying to

00:09:54.802 --> 00:09:56.593
buy goodwill with money is transparent.

00:09:56.593 --> 00:09:59.597
It will definitely cause even more scandal.

00:09:59.597 --> 00:10:02.617
Well, that was just a warm-up.

00:10:02.617 --> 00:10:05.525
Here is Dramatic Restoration Plan Two.

00:10:05.525 --> 00:10:08.300
Having a Celebrity Say That
O-Con Is an Amazing Person.

00:10:08.300 --> 00:10:10.789
- Like having Justin Bieber...
- Rejected.

00:10:10.789 --> 00:10:11.905
That's clearly staged.

00:10:11.905 --> 00:10:14.909
Besides, Justin Bieber
is not going to comment on my behalf.

00:10:14.909 --> 00:10:18.485
Then next... Well...

00:10:18.485 --> 00:10:21.325
- Can I pitch one?
- Me too...

00:10:21.325 --> 00:10:24.649
If you just disappear like this, we'd also...

00:10:25.309 --> 00:10:27.633
So here it is.

00:10:28.813 --> 00:10:32.393
Covering Up a Scandal with Another Scandal.

00:10:32.393 --> 00:10:37.241
People who love online scandals
thrive on fresh scandals.

00:10:37.241 --> 00:10:42.400
So if I'm at... pull out...,

00:10:42.400 --> 00:10:45.585
and get filmed on video by...

00:10:45.585 --> 00:10:46.625
Rejected.

00:10:46.625 --> 00:10:50.673
Would you consider entrusting
your company's management to me?

00:10:50.673 --> 00:10:51.769
Well...

00:10:51.769 --> 00:10:53.645
The character business is all about strategy.

00:10:53.645 --> 00:10:57.605
That's where I, Takumi Omishima, come in.

00:10:57.605 --> 00:10:59.709
If you leave it to me,

00:10:59.709 --> 00:11:00.829
[Making Sidelong Glance Section Chief]
I will make

00:11:00.829 --> 00:11:02.185
[Morimoto a National Character]
Sidelong Glance Section Chief Morimoto

00:11:02.185 --> 00:11:03.857
the next Hello Kitty.

00:11:03.857 --> 00:11:06.177
- Well...
- Hold on.

00:11:06.177 --> 00:11:09.293
If you grant me management rights,

00:11:09.293 --> 00:11:14.093
I will invest 100 million yen
into your company.

00:11:14.093 --> 00:11:15.233
How does that sound?

00:11:15.233 --> 00:11:17.593
Well...

00:11:23.389 --> 00:11:24.866
In exchange for me investing 100 million yen,

00:11:24.866 --> 00:11:27.649
will you let me manage your company?

00:11:27.649 --> 00:11:29.809
- No way, honestly.
- "Honestly"?

00:11:29.809 --> 00:11:32.645
I mean, you're that Omishima, right?

00:11:32.645 --> 00:11:34.933
Yes, I am that Takumi Omishima.

00:11:34.933 --> 00:11:37.425
Then, honestly, it's no way.

00:11:38.653 --> 00:11:40.581
"Honestly".

00:11:44.201 --> 00:11:45.737
All right!

00:11:45.737 --> 00:11:48.005
Dramatic Restoration Plan 98.

00:11:48.005 --> 00:11:50.105
Do an Extreme Apology.

00:11:50.105 --> 00:11:51.521
Not just prostrating on the floor.

00:11:51.521 --> 00:11:53.765
It's to the point where people
can't even tell if you're apologizing.

00:11:53.765 --> 00:11:55.609
Like what, for example?

00:11:57.393 --> 00:11:59.049
A toilet seat.

00:11:59.049 --> 00:12:00.313
- Rejected.
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:12:00.313 --> 00:12:02.413
People would probably just get mad at us.

00:12:02.413 --> 00:12:05.397
- All right, Dramatic Restoration Plan 99!
- Go ahead.

00:12:05.397 --> 00:12:07.913
You marry someone
and change your last name from Kusakabe.

00:12:07.913 --> 00:12:09.315
Then play dumb like,

00:12:09.315 --> 00:12:10.357
- "Who's that Ms. Kusakabe again?"
- Yeah.

00:12:10.357 --> 00:12:11.537
- Yes! That works!
- Yeah.

00:12:11.537 --> 00:12:13.925
- Totally works, right?
- Anna Seo.

00:12:13.925 --> 00:12:15.421
Rejected.

00:12:15.421 --> 00:12:17.766
Anything else?

00:12:18.525 --> 00:12:19.797
- Is there anything else?
- Excuse me.

00:12:19.797 --> 00:12:23.221
- Then...
- I see. So you're quitting.

00:12:23.221 --> 00:12:25.853
- Go ahead, go ahead.
- I'm the one to blame.

00:12:27.493 --> 00:12:30.697
- Your move.
- Well, what do you say?

00:12:30.697 --> 00:12:33.041
- Is that all?
- There's more, Mr. Hirose!

00:12:33.041 --> 00:12:35.385
So I said it's fine. Now, now, now, there is.

00:12:35.385 --> 00:12:37.625
- We have 600 more!
- Yes, that's right!

00:12:37.625 --> 00:12:39.825
- Mr. Hirose...
- That's more than enough.

00:12:39.825 --> 00:12:41.661
Thank you very much.

00:12:41.661 --> 00:12:46.633
Honestly, I'm so touched that you
came up with 99 plans for someone like me.

00:12:48.413 --> 00:12:50.868
Tomorrow, I'll go to the Ministry of Economy,
Trade and Industry

00:12:50.868 --> 00:12:53.037
and propose resigning.

00:12:53.037 --> 00:12:57.041
I'll do everything I can to beg them
to keep Tuesla as the ambassador.

00:12:57.041 --> 00:13:00.837
Maybe even with an extreme apology.

00:13:00.837 --> 00:13:02.889
All right!

00:13:11.561 --> 00:13:13.061
[Hakusendo Ad Agency Former Executive]

00:13:13.061 --> 00:13:14.921
[Yusuke Taira Appointed
New President of Merry Co., Ltd.]

00:13:16.313 --> 00:13:21.637
♪ Ah, if I don't cry at graduation ♪

00:13:21.637 --> 00:13:26.469
♪ People might say I'm cold-hearted ♪

00:13:26.469 --> 00:13:34.649
♪ But I'll save my tears for
even sadder moments ♪

00:13:34.649 --> 00:13:37.897
You don't have to force a smile.

00:13:37.897 --> 00:13:39.785
I'm not forcing it.

00:13:40.525 --> 00:13:42.685
Hey, let's sing some Morning Musume together.

00:13:42.685 --> 00:13:45.953
"Happy Summer Wedding". I'll be Nacchi.
What about you, Ms. Sasaoka?

00:13:45.953 --> 00:13:48.225
Speaking of weddings...

00:13:48.225 --> 00:13:51.497
What happened with that? Mr. Seo's proposal?

00:13:54.369 --> 00:13:57.897
To be honest, it's still up in the air.

00:14:00.297 --> 00:14:05.089
I've been watching Mr. Seo this whole time.

00:14:05.089 --> 00:14:11.361
Always, constantly, staring at him
whenever I had free time.

00:14:13.921 --> 00:14:15.629
So...

00:14:17.985 --> 00:14:19.961
So?

00:14:19.961 --> 00:14:23.677
I started thinking it might not be a bad idea
for the two of you to get married.

00:14:23.677 --> 00:14:26.161
Wait, really?

00:14:26.161 --> 00:14:28.229
I mean...

00:14:28.229 --> 00:14:30.109
Don't you like him?

00:14:30.109 --> 00:14:32.057
Well, yes.

00:14:32.057 --> 00:14:37.341
I wouldn't say my romantic feelings
for Mr. Seo are zero.

00:14:37.993 --> 00:14:42.113
But beyond those feelings,

00:14:42.113 --> 00:14:46.900
I love seeing him create things.

00:14:58.517 --> 00:15:00.353
And that's why

00:15:02.301 --> 00:15:07.869
I believe that as a creator,
Mr. Seo needs you.

00:15:07.869 --> 00:15:10.469
From a producer's perspective,

00:15:11.313 --> 00:15:17.021
I thought that marriage between
the two of you could actually work.

00:15:18.593 --> 00:15:20.557
But somehow...

00:15:22.753 --> 00:15:25.066
Anyway, putting all that aside...

00:15:30.585 --> 00:15:32.429
I'm going to miss you.

00:15:36.009 --> 00:15:39.861
I'll be so lonely without you.

00:15:43.605 --> 00:15:47.533
And I'm sure that Mr. Seo
and Mr. Hirose feel the same way.

00:15:49.581 --> 00:15:51.441
Ms. Kusakabe,

00:15:52.757 --> 00:15:55.185
are you really okay with this?

00:15:56.069 --> 00:15:59.029
I really want to work with you more.

00:16:00.689 --> 00:16:02.677
For Tuesla's sake,

00:16:04.009 --> 00:16:07.069
the four of us, together, like we always do.

00:16:19.445 --> 00:16:21.345
I'm so happy.

00:16:23.449 --> 00:16:26.001
Hearing you say that,

00:16:26.757 --> 00:16:28.661
it truly makes me so happy.

00:16:34.745 --> 00:16:38.733
Thank you, Ms. Sasaoka.

00:16:42.445 --> 00:16:47.661
Well, I need to go get ready,
so I'll be leaving now.

00:16:48.429 --> 00:16:51.481
Oh, right.

00:16:51.481 --> 00:16:53.537
Why don't we take a photo?

00:16:53.537 --> 00:16:54.937
Okay? Let's do it!

00:16:54.937 --> 00:16:57.001
You too, Ms. Sasaoka!
Let's take a photo together!

00:16:57.001 --> 00:16:59.937
Come on. Don't make that face.

00:16:59.937 --> 00:17:01.797
Frowning makes you look older.

00:17:01.797 --> 00:17:03.593
Come over here. Come on.

00:17:03.593 --> 00:17:05.085
Oh, Mr. Seo, get Tuesla!

00:17:05.085 --> 00:17:06.693
- Bring Tuesla over!
- Oh, Tuesla.

00:17:06.693 --> 00:17:10.645
Ready? Lift the corners of
your mouth! Big smiles!

00:17:10.645 --> 00:17:15.745
Ready, set. Tu-Tu-Tu's Tu! Smile!

00:17:27.613 --> 00:17:32.153
Good for you. You're going
to be an ambassador.

00:17:32.153 --> 00:17:34.933
Now people all over the world can...

00:17:43.029 --> 00:17:44.925
Hey.

00:17:44.925 --> 00:17:47.105
When that happens,

00:17:47.105 --> 00:17:49.733
where will O-Con be,
and what will she be doing?

00:17:57.389 --> 00:18:01.929
Will we still be able to smile
like we're doing here?

00:18:29.477 --> 00:18:31.261
All right.

00:18:33.465 --> 00:18:35.337
Please.

00:18:37.049 --> 00:18:39.285
I think it's good.

00:18:39.285 --> 00:18:42.665
- I'm all for it.
- Me too.

00:18:45.241 --> 00:18:47.041
Thank you.

00:18:51.361 --> 00:18:53.221
Sorry.

00:19:30.801 --> 00:19:32.433
[METI Buildings]
Neither Seo Design

00:19:32.433 --> 00:19:34.797
nor Mizuki Seo bears any responsibility.

00:19:34.797 --> 00:19:38.837
As of today, my consulting contract
with Seo Design has been terminated.

00:19:38.837 --> 00:19:42.466
- I myself... In other words...
- Well, Ms. Kusakabe...

00:19:42.466 --> 00:19:44.421
Concentrate all the sparks of the scandal

00:19:44.421 --> 00:19:45.849
- on me alone.
- Ms. Kusakabe.

00:19:45.849 --> 00:19:48.449
Mr. Hatoishi, I'm begging you.

00:19:48.449 --> 00:19:51.541
Please let Tuesla be the Expo Ambassador.

00:19:51.541 --> 00:19:56.769
Actually, Mr. Seo was here
just a little while ago.

00:19:56.769 --> 00:19:58.093
What?

00:19:58.093 --> 00:20:00.900
He declined the ambassador appointment.

00:20:02.625 --> 00:20:04.466
What's the meaning of this?

00:20:07.813 --> 00:20:11.793
This way, you don't have to quit.

00:20:12.629 --> 00:20:14.369
Wait a minute.

00:20:14.369 --> 00:20:16.605
Without the ambassador deal,

00:20:16.605 --> 00:20:19.797
we don't need to
put out the fire immediately.

00:20:19.797 --> 00:20:22.607
You don't get it. Being the Expo Ambassador
is such an opportunity

00:20:22.607 --> 00:20:25.233
- to reach the world...
- That kind of thing

00:20:26.053 --> 00:20:28.717
is pointless unless it's with O-Con.

00:20:28.717 --> 00:20:31.397
Over such a childish reason?

00:20:32.133 --> 00:20:34.261
Is it really that strange?

00:20:34.261 --> 00:20:36.305
Not wanting to do it without you?

00:20:39.161 --> 00:20:40.937
Tuesla is something

00:20:41.985 --> 00:20:44.597
we thought up together,

00:20:44.597 --> 00:20:46.509
created together,

00:20:47.173 --> 00:20:49.033
and raised together.

00:20:51.597 --> 00:20:54.697
And I want to share all the fun
that's to come with you too.

00:20:55.465 --> 00:20:57.377
Is wanting that really so strange?

00:20:59.537 --> 00:21:03.809
I don't want you to leave my side.

00:21:17.765 --> 00:21:19.500
O-Con.

00:21:23.881 --> 00:21:25.689
Marry me.

00:21:27.106 --> 00:21:30.085
You don't have to answer right away.

00:21:38.665 --> 00:21:40.409
Let's head back.

00:21:59.165 --> 00:22:01.100
Everything's going to be fine.

00:22:06.333 --> 00:22:07.497
We're back.

00:22:07.497 --> 00:22:09.966
- Welcome back.
- Welcome back.

00:22:11.585 --> 00:22:13.805
Ms. Kusakabe!

00:22:13.805 --> 00:22:16.149
- Welcome back.
- Welcome back.

00:22:16.149 --> 00:22:19.465
I'm sorry for coming back.

00:22:19.465 --> 00:22:22.357
- Why are you apologizing?
- Don't say that.

00:22:23.841 --> 00:22:27.600
Actually, we need to talk.
Do you have a moment?

00:22:29.765 --> 00:22:33.465
Our losses this month are
200 million yen in the red.

00:22:33.465 --> 00:22:36.681
The returns are all because of me.
I'm so sorry.

00:22:36.681 --> 00:22:40.821
At this rate, cash flow will
run dry in three months.

00:22:40.821 --> 00:22:44.213
And as of right now, we don't have
any plan to revive Tuesla.

00:22:44.213 --> 00:22:47.181
So what do we need to do right now?

00:22:47.181 --> 00:22:50.133
Cut costs drastically.

00:22:50.133 --> 00:22:51.945
Which is why...

00:22:53.433 --> 00:22:54.733
[Letter of Resignation]

00:22:54.733 --> 00:22:57.485
We're resigning from Seo Design.

00:22:58.905 --> 00:23:01.105
- What?
- Seo Design is

00:23:01.105 --> 00:23:05.125
a wonderful company
that cherishes its employees,

00:23:05.125 --> 00:23:07.761
but if the company goes under,
it defeats the whole point.

00:23:07.761 --> 00:23:09.281
You can't do that! I should be the one to...

00:23:09.281 --> 00:23:14.221
Ms. Kusakabe, you are essential to Mr. Seo
and to reviving Tuesla.

00:23:14.221 --> 00:23:16.657
But both of you are essential too,
Ms. Sasaoka and Mr. Hirose!

00:23:16.657 --> 00:23:17.849
This makes no sense!

00:23:17.849 --> 00:23:21.785
If it's a big company, even if they
temporarily suspend Tuesla's activities,

00:23:21.785 --> 00:23:24.497
there'd still be a chance for a comeback.

00:23:24.497 --> 00:23:27.949
But in our case, bankruptcy is the end.

00:23:27.949 --> 00:23:29.713
Tuesla will be gone forever.

00:23:29.713 --> 00:23:33.389
So the two of you have to protect it.

00:23:33.389 --> 00:23:35.637
Rejected! No way! Absolutely not!

00:23:35.637 --> 00:23:38.685
We have the right to resign.

00:23:47.029 --> 00:23:50.081
Actually, we've already
lined up our next jobs.

00:23:50.081 --> 00:23:51.609
Right?

00:23:51.609 --> 00:23:54.341
So please...

00:23:58.285 --> 00:24:00.061
Mr. Seo,

00:24:01.489 --> 00:24:03.357
Ms. Kusakabe,

00:24:04.929 --> 00:24:06.639
please ensure that

00:24:07.653 --> 00:24:10.457
Tuesla can still be loved by someone

00:24:11.869 --> 00:24:13.741
fifty years from now.

00:24:20.165 --> 00:24:22.821
- Please take care of it.
- Please.

00:24:24.501 --> 00:24:28.749
- What about new designs for Molco?
- What do you think?

00:24:28.749 --> 00:24:32.041
- Rainbow!
- Rainbow Molco sounds adorable!

00:24:35.801 --> 00:24:40.765
- Magical Molco!
- Magical Molco would be great!

00:24:40.765 --> 00:24:43.681
Sorry for calling you over here so suddenly.

00:24:43.681 --> 00:24:47.093
All my hometown tax donation gifts
arrived at the same time,

00:24:47.093 --> 00:24:49.569
and I was like, "I can't eat all this alone!"

00:24:50.649 --> 00:24:53.949
Hometown tax donation gifts?

00:24:53.949 --> 00:24:58.409
Though all of these are also sold at
the supermarket by the train station.

00:25:01.373 --> 00:25:06.469
So, do you want to forget all the bad stuff
and just have fun drinking?

00:25:06.469 --> 00:25:11.169
Or are you in the mood to vent to someone?

00:25:18.077 --> 00:25:20.453
Because of my scandal,

00:25:21.173 --> 00:25:24.833
my cherished colleagues
at Seo Design had to resign.

00:25:25.637 --> 00:25:30.621
Mr. Hirose and Ms. Sasaoka truly love Tuesla,

00:25:30.621 --> 00:25:33.089
and they always gave Tuesla
everything they had.

00:25:34.321 --> 00:25:36.589
Why did people like them have to...

00:25:36.589 --> 00:25:40.069
But don't you love Tuesla just as much?

00:25:40.069 --> 00:25:41.973
I...

00:25:44.481 --> 00:25:45.961
I...

00:25:45.961 --> 00:25:48.361
Huh? Is that not the case?

00:25:49.849 --> 00:25:53.717
Come on. Just let it out. Say it.

00:25:53.717 --> 00:25:56.805
At times like this, it's best to just
say everything that's on your mind.

00:25:56.805 --> 00:26:00.209
Even if it's messy or rude,
just spit it out. Come on.

00:26:00.209 --> 00:26:04.725
I'm way messier and ruder
than you anyway, right?

00:26:04.725 --> 00:26:06.437
Come on.

00:26:10.673 --> 00:26:12.873
When Mr. Seo told me

00:26:14.085 --> 00:26:16.139
he wanted me to stay
even if it meant turning down

00:26:16.139 --> 00:26:18.345
the Expo Ambassador role for Tuesla,

00:26:18.981 --> 00:26:20.977
my heart wavered,

00:26:22.049 --> 00:26:24.641
and I couldn't help but feel happy.

00:26:26.621 --> 00:26:29.661
Even though he lost a huge opportunity
because of me.

00:26:31.033 --> 00:26:33.009
Isn't that just...

00:26:34.301 --> 00:26:36.121
Isn't that what?

00:26:37.701 --> 00:26:39.473
Isn't that

00:26:41.357 --> 00:26:44.005
truly the worst?

00:26:44.005 --> 00:26:48.006
Doesn't that make me a selfish,
self-centered monster?

00:26:51.821 --> 00:26:54.589
Mr. Hirose and Ms. Sasaoka are giving up

00:26:54.589 --> 00:27:00.741
the Tuesla they love so much
just to protect it.

00:27:03.909 --> 00:27:05.749
And yet I...

00:27:07.549 --> 00:27:09.325
I just...

00:27:10.669 --> 00:27:12.645
I hate it so much.

00:27:14.941 --> 00:27:16.757
I really hate this.

00:27:18.825 --> 00:27:20.613
There, there.

00:27:20.613 --> 00:27:22.941
You got it all out.

00:27:22.941 --> 00:27:25.277
Right? Feeling better now?

00:27:26.113 --> 00:27:29.557
So basically, you're the worst,

00:27:29.557 --> 00:27:32.741
and those two are the absolute best, right?

00:27:34.225 --> 00:27:36.666
So? What are you going to do?

00:27:39.361 --> 00:27:44.809
Those two amazing people told you
that you're the one

00:27:44.809 --> 00:27:48.313
who needs to stay for Tuesla, right?

00:27:48.313 --> 00:27:51.549
They believed in you, didn't they?

00:27:51.549 --> 00:27:53.333
Here, drink up.

00:27:55.233 --> 00:27:59.333
Wash it all down with this.

00:27:59.997 --> 00:28:01.744
Okay?

00:28:03.029 --> 00:28:04.805
Okay.

00:28:05.553 --> 00:28:07.266
There, there, there.

00:28:08.373 --> 00:28:09.617
[Scandal-Free Advertising Tactics;
How Companies Rebound?]

00:28:09.617 --> 00:28:10.860
[From Scandal Response to Dialogue]

00:28:10.860 --> 00:28:12.100
[Conveying Facts and Stance
Instead of Just Apologizing...]

00:28:13.017 --> 00:28:14.825
[Don't Leave Behind Those
Who Loved Tutu-Tuesla]

00:28:19.501 --> 00:28:21.433
[Executives with a Track Record
in Design; High-Intent Investors]

00:28:23.929 --> 00:28:25.165
Hello, Mr. Fuchinobe?

00:28:25.165 --> 00:28:28.205
About the "Rebuilding After PR Scandals"
case studies you asked for,

00:28:28.205 --> 00:28:30.085
I put together a quick summary
and sent it over.

00:28:30.085 --> 00:28:33.085
Thanks. Let me treat you to
some barbecue next time.

00:28:33.085 --> 00:28:37.053
And it looks like this guy
needs a scandal recovery plan too.

00:28:37.053 --> 00:28:38.066
[Sent: "Rebuilding After PR Scandals"]
Huh?

00:28:38.066 --> 00:28:39.169
[Former Merry President
Takumi Omishima: Power Harassment]

00:28:39.169 --> 00:28:40.209
[Unauthorized Design Alterations,
and Multiple Misconducts!]

00:28:40.209 --> 00:28:41.261
[Former President Omishima:
Cynical Molco was designed]

00:28:41.261 --> 00:28:42.281
[through deception
and altered without permission]

00:28:42.281 --> 00:28:43.385
[Wait, unauthorized alterations?]
The comments

00:28:43.385 --> 00:28:44.797
[That's insane...]
are blowing up pretty badly.

00:28:44.797 --> 00:28:46.593
[It makes me sick to think that
I bought products from someone like him]

00:28:50.881 --> 00:28:53.169
- Yeah, exactly.
- Isn't that Mr. Omishima?

00:28:53.169 --> 00:28:54.925
Yeah, it is.

00:28:58.493 --> 00:29:00.509
Wow, isn't that crazy?

00:29:05.910 --> 00:29:07.685
- Look, it's Tuesla.
- Tuesla.

00:29:07.685 --> 00:29:10.281
Did you see the one that's scandal-hit?
The consulting video?

00:29:10.281 --> 00:29:11.829
Yeah, yeah, I saw that consulting video.

00:29:11.829 --> 00:29:14.233
- That's crazy.
- It's Tuesla!

00:29:16.073 --> 00:29:18.033
So cute!

00:29:25.873 --> 00:29:28.637
Don't you want to bring the two of them back?

00:29:29.869 --> 00:29:33.913
Don't you want to restore Seo Design
to what it used to be?

00:29:36.093 --> 00:29:38.057
Can we really do that?

00:29:38.057 --> 00:29:41.245
Yes, as long as we have an investor.

00:29:41.245 --> 00:29:42.673
An investor?

00:29:42.673 --> 00:29:46.965
A person or company that
will provide funds to Seo Design.

00:29:46.965 --> 00:29:49.766
But who would put up money for us right now?

00:29:49.766 --> 00:29:51.925
I've already found someone.

00:29:51.925 --> 00:29:55.449
They're willing to invest 10 million yen.

00:29:55.449 --> 00:29:57.597
- 10 million?
- With that much,

00:29:57.597 --> 00:29:59.973
we can bring Mr. Hirose and Ms. Sasaoka back

00:29:59.973 --> 00:30:02.853
and secure operating funds
until Tuesla is revived.

00:30:02.853 --> 00:30:05.785
In return, we will have to
hand over management,

00:30:05.785 --> 00:30:08.100
but you will still retain final
decision-making power.

00:30:09.793 --> 00:30:12.041
Our investor has arrived.

00:30:12.041 --> 00:30:14.200
What? The 10 million yen? Already?

00:30:15.329 --> 00:30:18.033
- It's a pleasure to have you here.
- It's a pleasure to...

00:30:21.269 --> 00:30:23.129
What are you doing here?

00:30:30.793 --> 00:30:34.933
Oh? Where are the two who betrayed me?

00:30:36.641 --> 00:30:38.533
Did they abandon you, by any chance?

00:30:38.533 --> 00:30:41.466
No. They'll be back soon.

00:30:41.466 --> 00:30:44.549
Oh? So you have the money to bring them back?

00:30:44.549 --> 00:30:46.833
Where is it?

00:30:48.021 --> 00:30:50.049
Rejected! Negotiation over!

00:30:50.049 --> 00:30:52.117
So you're giving up, then?

00:30:52.117 --> 00:30:54.681
Giving up on Mr. Hirose and Ms. Sasaoka?

00:30:54.681 --> 00:30:58.166
This is all for our team, and for Tuesla.

00:31:02.305 --> 00:31:06.281
Can you do it like this?
Aren't you supposed to be begging me?

00:31:06.281 --> 00:31:09.953
- Beg you?
- You need my money, don't you?

00:31:09.953 --> 00:31:15.233
So obviously you need to ask.
You need to beg.

00:31:18.349 --> 00:31:21.369
All right, repeat after me and beg.

00:31:21.369 --> 00:31:25.029
"Mr. Omishima, please invest in us."

00:31:25.029 --> 00:31:27.465
Mr. Omishima, please invest in us.

00:31:27.465 --> 00:31:31.997
"I was wrong about everything,
and Mr. Omishima was right."

00:31:31.997 --> 00:31:34.845
I was wrong about everything,

00:31:34.845 --> 00:31:41.649
and Mr. Omishima...
Mr. Omishima was r-r-right...

00:31:41.649 --> 00:31:45.153
By the way, I heard something
from a junior colleague.

00:31:45.153 --> 00:31:49.609
Mr. Omishima, lately you've been
meeting with multiple companies,

00:31:49.609 --> 00:31:51.733
trying to acquire management rights
in exchange for investments, right?

00:31:51.733 --> 00:31:55.493
And they all turned you down.

00:31:55.493 --> 00:32:00.369
A company that'd negotiate with you like this
while you're caught in a scandal,

00:32:00.369 --> 00:32:04.125
there's no one left but us, right?

00:32:05.345 --> 00:32:09.433
So in that case, you should
stop making one-sided demands.

00:32:09.433 --> 00:32:13.745
Well now, looks like the tables
have turned. Go on, beg...

00:32:13.745 --> 00:32:16.657
We are in a similar position.

00:32:16.657 --> 00:32:20.849
Not only are we broke,
but our scandal is still ongoing.

00:32:20.849 --> 00:32:24.666
That is why we should use Mr. Omishima.

00:32:25.361 --> 00:32:30.533
All of Japan knows that Mr. Omishima
is in a tight spot right now.

00:32:30.533 --> 00:32:32.189
If Mr. Seo, who has a history
with Mr. Omishima,

00:32:32.189 --> 00:32:35.993
forgives Mr. Omishima
and extends a helping hand,

00:32:35.993 --> 00:32:39.793
Mr. Seo will go from a scandal-hit
fake prince to a kind-hearted hero.

00:32:39.793 --> 00:32:41.053
But this guy...

00:32:41.053 --> 00:32:44.029
You should both show
a willingness to compromise.

00:32:44.029 --> 00:32:47.641
Compromise? Me? With Lie-mishima?

00:32:49.625 --> 00:32:51.600
It's for Tuesla.

00:33:04.833 --> 00:33:06.733
For Tuesla...

00:33:09.109 --> 00:33:11.277
- What?
- Wait, wait, wait!

00:33:11.277 --> 00:33:12.669
Please wait! Why the sudden change?

00:33:12.669 --> 00:33:15.689
Because it's become crystal clear that
working with you two is impossible.

00:33:15.689 --> 00:33:19.133
Huh? Why? I was just
getting ready to compromise!

00:33:19.133 --> 00:33:21.553
That right there.

00:33:21.553 --> 00:33:26.249
The way you'd do anything
just to protect what you love,

00:33:26.249 --> 00:33:27.829
and how you immerse yourself
in your own world

00:33:27.829 --> 00:33:29.129
without caring what others think.

00:33:29.129 --> 00:33:33.381
Watching that makes my skin crawl.

00:33:33.381 --> 00:33:34.545
What are you talking about?

00:33:34.545 --> 00:33:39.466
I utterly loathe passionate crazies
like you two

00:33:39.466 --> 00:33:42.873
who lose their minds over what they love.

00:33:42.873 --> 00:33:44.077
What?

00:33:44.077 --> 00:33:48.200
Always acting like you're
the only ones in the right.

00:33:48.821 --> 00:33:52.081
I've always wondered about this.

00:33:52.081 --> 00:33:53.621
No matter what movie or drama I watch,

00:33:53.621 --> 00:33:55.825
it's always passionate crazies
like you who are the protagonists.

00:33:55.825 --> 00:33:57.177
Why is that?

00:33:57.177 --> 00:34:01.265
In reality, you're just complete nuisances.

00:34:03.193 --> 00:34:05.313
I see.

00:34:06.089 --> 00:34:08.166
My grandma used to say that

00:34:08.166 --> 00:34:10.109
people who have nothing that
they're passionate about

00:34:10.109 --> 00:34:13.205
are as common as people
who eat bread for breakfast.

00:34:13.205 --> 00:34:16.425
That's you, isn't it?
You don't have anything you love.

00:34:18.353 --> 00:34:20.321
Whatever, it's totally fine.

00:34:20.321 --> 00:34:22.733
Right? Nothing wrong with that, right?

00:34:22.733 --> 00:34:27.861
Who said that? Who said that
I have nothing I love?

00:34:29.301 --> 00:34:33.709
There's no such person.
Not a single one in this world!

00:34:33.709 --> 00:34:36.529
Well... but I didn't have anything
I liked before either.

00:34:36.529 --> 00:34:39.700
Then let me ask you,
do you like melon? Do you like it?

00:34:39.700 --> 00:34:42.509
Melon? Well, I guess.

00:34:42.509 --> 00:34:44.069
See?

00:34:44.069 --> 00:34:46.437
Some love meat, some love games,
some love clothes.

00:34:46.437 --> 00:34:48.397
Everyone has things they like!

00:34:48.397 --> 00:34:53.237
Yet people like you make it impossible

00:34:53.237 --> 00:34:55.533
for me to even talk about my small likes!

00:34:55.533 --> 00:34:58.237
What?

00:34:58.237 --> 00:35:00.937
How did I ever stop you from
talking about what you like?

00:35:00.937 --> 00:35:04.613
Most people's passion level is a 10 or below!

00:35:04.613 --> 00:35:06.181
Even if they like meat, they'll eat fish.

00:35:06.181 --> 00:35:07.785
Even if they like gaming,
they'll go to sleep when tired.

00:35:07.785 --> 00:35:09.221
That's not real passion.

00:35:09.221 --> 00:35:11.881
Yes, it is!

00:35:11.881 --> 00:35:17.881
It might be small and feeble,
easily overshadowed by other things,

00:35:17.881 --> 00:35:22.800
but it's still passion!

00:35:26.661 --> 00:35:28.949
Back in high school,

00:35:28.949 --> 00:35:31.501
[Drama Club]
I once became interested in acting.

00:35:31.501 --> 00:35:34.145
[Recruiting Members]
Then the acting crazies

00:35:34.145 --> 00:35:37.133
- invited me to join them.
- Let's do it.

00:35:37.133 --> 00:35:38.713
I was looking for you!

00:35:38.713 --> 00:35:41.653
They fasted and stayed up all night

00:35:41.653 --> 00:35:45.201
just because they were playing
sick patients. In the end...

00:35:45.201 --> 00:35:47.621
- Oh, that was super realistic.
- I was completely repulsed.

00:35:47.621 --> 00:35:51.409
And after that, I could
no longer say that I liked acting.

00:35:51.409 --> 00:35:53.093
[Gospel Club]
In college,

00:35:53.093 --> 00:35:55.745
I took an interest in gospel music.

00:35:55.745 --> 00:35:56.921
Are you interested in gospel?

00:35:56.921 --> 00:35:58.037
- Let's do it together!
- Come sing with us!

00:35:58.037 --> 00:35:59.317
Let's do it!

00:35:59.317 --> 00:36:03.533
- They sang and harmonized everywhere.
- ♪ Hallelujah ♪

00:36:03.533 --> 00:36:05.133
I couldn't keep up.

00:36:05.133 --> 00:36:09.033
And I could no longer say
that I liked gospel music.

00:36:09.033 --> 00:36:11.041
Later, I got into oden.

00:36:11.041 --> 00:36:13.045
- You like oden?
- Right now I'm eating radish...

00:36:13.045 --> 00:36:15.433
- Radish!
- Radish!

00:36:15.433 --> 00:36:18.661
They even ate scalding-hot oden
under the scorching sun.

00:36:18.661 --> 00:36:23.129
And I could no longer say that I liked oden.

00:36:23.129 --> 00:36:25.017
It's always like that.

00:36:25.017 --> 00:36:29.517
People like you with passion levels over 90
always stifle what I like.

00:36:29.517 --> 00:36:32.253
Then just say it. Nobody's stopping you.

00:36:32.253 --> 00:36:34.045
You don't get it at all, do you?

00:36:34.045 --> 00:36:36.933
You give off an atmosphere that
makes it impossible to speak up!

00:36:36.933 --> 00:36:40.145
As if to say, "That's not real passion!"

00:36:40.145 --> 00:36:43.837
With nothing in particular
that I wanted to do,

00:36:43.837 --> 00:36:45.933
I randomly started a business.

00:36:45.933 --> 00:36:49.993
Then numbers appeared
as a whole different measure.

00:36:49.993 --> 00:36:51.965
I clung to it.

00:36:51.965 --> 00:36:53.713
Because without passion,
I could still be praised

00:36:53.713 --> 00:36:55.745
and call myself happy.

00:36:55.745 --> 00:36:57.805
But then...

00:36:57.805 --> 00:37:00.913
came a man who doesn't think twice
when it's for what he loves,

00:37:00.913 --> 00:37:04.081
a level-100 lover.

00:37:04.081 --> 00:37:07.249
- I could never acknowledge him.
- You're Mr. Seo,

00:37:07.249 --> 00:37:08.749
- I thought that
- the designer. Right?

00:37:08.749 --> 00:37:11.197
- if I acknowledged this man,
- Did you hear me?

00:37:11.197 --> 00:37:14.933
I'd be back to being empty.

00:37:15.905 --> 00:37:21.049
You force your passion
inferiority complex onto me.

00:37:21.757 --> 00:37:25.589
Don't just cast me as the perpetrator!

00:37:25.589 --> 00:37:27.105
Mr. Seo.

00:37:27.105 --> 00:37:28.873
Is it painful, not having anything you love?

00:37:28.873 --> 00:37:30.605
Sure, people like you often say that

00:37:30.605 --> 00:37:32.615
you envy those who have something
to be passionate about.

00:37:32.615 --> 00:37:35.181
But you know what? I've caught on!

00:37:35.181 --> 00:37:37.949
Deep in your eyes,
you're thinking, "He's a freak."

00:37:37.949 --> 00:37:40.685
I know that's how you look at me!

00:37:40.685 --> 00:37:44.081
If that's how you're going to put it,
then I've been a victim all along too.

00:37:44.081 --> 00:37:48.433
And people like you
are the real perpetrators!

00:37:52.461 --> 00:37:56.193
You could never understand how I feel.

00:37:58.425 --> 00:38:02.145
Unfortunately, it seems the deal is off.

00:38:03.285 --> 00:38:05.061
No.

00:38:05.781 --> 00:38:10.265
I am convinced now more than ever
that we should make a deal.

00:38:12.117 --> 00:38:15.537
Actually, I went to a merchandise shop
the other day.

00:38:15.537 --> 00:38:16.721
It's Tuesla.

00:38:16.721 --> 00:38:17.813
There,

00:38:17.813 --> 00:38:21.337
- I saw a girl adoring Tuesla.
- So cute!

00:38:21.337 --> 00:38:23.589
I was truly happy,

00:38:23.589 --> 00:38:25.189
- but to that girl,
- This one

00:38:25.189 --> 00:38:27.609
- Tuesla wasn't special.
- is also so cute!

00:38:27.609 --> 00:38:29.469
- Same as other plushies,
- There, there.

00:38:29.469 --> 00:38:31.937
it's just an ordinary fondness.

00:38:31.937 --> 00:38:36.061
Even so, it still made me so happy.

00:38:36.061 --> 00:38:40.205
Even if it wasn't a special kind of love,
just an ordinary fondness,

00:38:40.205 --> 00:38:43.937
it somehow cheered me up.

00:38:43.937 --> 00:38:48.293
That's why, even if love
comes in different amounts,

00:38:48.293 --> 00:38:52.305
I don't believe that one
is superior to another.

00:38:52.305 --> 00:38:56.125
To Tuesla, those who give it
a huge amount of love

00:38:56.125 --> 00:39:01.117
and those who give it a small amount of love
are both precious.

00:39:01.117 --> 00:39:04.617
That's why you, Mr. Seo,
with a passion level of 100,

00:39:04.617 --> 00:39:07.077
and you, Mr. Omishima,
with a passion level of 1

00:39:07.077 --> 00:39:09.189
need each other.

00:39:09.889 --> 00:39:13.889
By acting as the gas pedal
and brake for each other,

00:39:13.889 --> 00:39:18.301
you can expand possibilities even further.

00:39:23.801 --> 00:39:25.957
I refuse.

00:39:33.886 --> 00:39:35.541
What's that guy doing?

00:39:35.541 --> 00:39:37.857
Gross! For a guy, that's weird.

00:39:37.857 --> 00:39:40.297
That kind of thing? Boo!

00:39:48.937 --> 00:39:50.865
I get it.

00:39:54.989 --> 00:40:00.133
You said earlier that I could
never understand your feelings,

00:40:00.781 --> 00:40:02.481
but I get it.

00:40:02.481 --> 00:40:05.529
I get it, just a little bit.

00:40:05.529 --> 00:40:06.753
Get what?

00:40:06.753 --> 00:40:09.845
Your passion was too small to talk about.

00:40:09.845 --> 00:40:13.709
And mine was too big to talk about.

00:40:13.709 --> 00:40:16.293
That kind of passion
you can't put into words,

00:40:16.293 --> 00:40:20.433
that feeling, I at least get that.

00:40:21.973 --> 00:40:28.089
And for the first time,
I kind of resonated with you.

00:40:28.089 --> 00:40:33.497
And inside me, that feeling
that you talked about...

00:40:33.497 --> 00:40:37.377
What are you mumbling about?
You're wasting time.

00:40:37.377 --> 00:40:39.125
I like you!

00:40:40.377 --> 00:40:43.541
I like you, Omishima.

00:40:43.541 --> 00:40:45.265
Huh? What?

00:40:45.265 --> 00:40:47.766
- I like you.
- Stop it.

00:40:48.477 --> 00:40:52.200
When I resonated with you just now,

00:40:53.465 --> 00:40:58.433
just a little bit, like, only level 1, but...

00:40:59.709 --> 00:41:01.501
I like you.

00:41:02.733 --> 00:41:04.266
Mr. Seo.

00:41:04.266 --> 00:41:09.697
Whether it's big love or small love,

00:41:09.697 --> 00:41:11.853
I want to create a world
where it's okay to say whatever.

00:41:11.853 --> 00:41:14.833
A world like that, with Tuesla,

00:41:15.873 --> 00:41:18.633
O-Con, and...

00:41:20.585 --> 00:41:22.361
And you.

00:41:22.361 --> 00:41:24.189
So, well,

00:41:24.189 --> 00:41:26.565
if you ever feel like it,

00:41:26.565 --> 00:41:28.577
just go with that.

00:41:42.273 --> 00:41:44.209
Thanks.

00:41:44.209 --> 00:41:46.009
There you are!

00:42:09.209 --> 00:42:11.505
If you sit there,
Mr. Seo will get mad at you again.

00:42:11.505 --> 00:42:15.429
This seat belongs to me,
the supreme authority here.

00:42:15.429 --> 00:42:17.971
But the final say belongs to

00:42:17.971 --> 00:42:20.997
- Mr. Seo, you know...
- More importantly,

00:42:20.997 --> 00:42:25.137
the finances here are in
even worse shape than I thought.

00:42:26.337 --> 00:42:28.165
I'm sorry.

00:42:32.697 --> 00:42:36.500
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:42:38.333 --> 00:42:41.073
- I'm Takaaki Hirose.
- I'm Suzuka Sasaoka.

00:42:41.073 --> 00:42:43.166
- We're back!
- We're back!

00:42:43.166 --> 00:42:45.665
I'm going to have you work hard.

00:42:45.665 --> 00:42:47.253
- Okay.
- Okay.

00:42:47.253 --> 00:42:49.845
Wait, isn't Ms. Kusakabe supposed to be here?

00:42:49.845 --> 00:42:50.897
I thought so too, but...

00:42:50.897 --> 00:42:52.949
What are you daydreaming about?

00:42:52.949 --> 00:42:54.921
[Notice of Contract Termination]
She quit.

00:42:54.921 --> 00:42:56.169
- What?
- Huh?

00:42:56.169 --> 00:42:57.961
Wait, why?

00:43:00.401 --> 00:43:04.101
Save the dumbfounded look for after your run.

00:43:10.381 --> 00:43:12.233
This makes no sense!

00:43:24.705 --> 00:43:26.961
There's no way you'd just quit.

00:43:26.961 --> 00:43:28.841
We were just getting started.

00:43:28.841 --> 00:43:29.949
From here on, together,

00:43:29.949 --> 00:43:33.533
- we bring Tuesla back...
- Shouldn't you listen to the reason first?

00:43:38.981 --> 00:43:40.885
Because I hate it.

00:43:41.929 --> 00:43:44.000
I truly, utterly hate it.

00:43:45.841 --> 00:43:48.989
I only ever saw you as a coworker,

00:43:48.989 --> 00:43:52.805
so talking about love and marriage
really disgusts me.

00:43:52.805 --> 00:43:58.921
And now that you've said it,
even if I turn you down,

00:43:58.921 --> 00:44:02.745
I don't think we can ever just
go back to how things were.

00:44:02.745 --> 00:44:06.145
Your selfish feelings

00:44:06.145 --> 00:44:09.285
robbed me of the job I loved.

00:44:13.557 --> 00:44:15.985
Goodbye.

00:44:15.985 --> 00:44:18.133
I don't think we'll ever meet again.